.TH "CHECK_HTML" "1" "April 2026" "NMS_Tools" "HTTP/HTTPS Content and Response Validator"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
\f[B]check_html\f[R] \[em] HTTP/HTTPS inspection and content validation
tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]check_html\f[R] -H [-p ] options
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]check_html\f[R] performs deterministic HTTP/HTTPS checks, including
status code validation, redirect chain capture, TLS negotiation details,
and optional content validation.
.PP
It is designed for: - Monitoring web services
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Detecting regressions
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Validating expected content
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Automation pipelines
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Target
.PP
\f[B]-H, \[en]host \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Target hostname.
.PP
\f[B]-p, \[en]port \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Port (default: 80 for HTTP, 443 for HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]\[en]path \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Request path.
.SS Validation
.PP
\f[B]\[en]expect-status \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Require specific HTTP status.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]expect-contains \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Require substring in response body.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]expect-json\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Validate JSON structure.
.SS Debugging
.PP
\f[B]\[en]debug-http\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Show request/response details.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]verbose\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Show redirect chain and timing metrics.
.SS Output Modes
.PP
\f[B]\[en]json\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Emit structured JSON.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]quiet\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Suppress human-readable output.
.SH EXIT CODES
.PP
\f[B]0\f[R] \[em] All checks passed
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]1\f[R] \[em] Non-critical deviation
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]2\f[R] \[em] Critical failure
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]3\f[R] \[em] Unknown error
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check homepage:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
check_html -H example.com
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Validate content:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
check_html -H example.com --expect-contains \[dq]Welcome\[dq]
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Debug HTTP:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
check_html -H api.example.com --debug-http
\f[R]
.fi
